WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.970
- Is it true that even
after all that time,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.768
that you still get mistaken
for Mila Kunis? Is that real?

00:00:04.768 --> 00:00:07.330
- I do, it still happens.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:10.500
I mean, I met her maybe 10 years ago.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.140
I was very excited to meet her.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.120
I was such a massive fan and
everyone always told me that I

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.173
looked like her.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.573
And, but the first time I
met her, she was like, I,

00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:24.220
I get confused as you all
the time. And I love it.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.000
I take it as a compliment
because you're younger than I am.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.890
So sometimes I go along with
it and I was like, well,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.356
the next time that I get mistaken for you,

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:36.670
can I pretend to be you?
And she gave me permission,

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.320
but then a month later
it was the Golden Globes

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.300
when she was nominated for black Swan.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.133
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.483
Tell them, you totally
acted like you were her.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.273
Please.

00:00:47.273 --> 00:00:51.963
- I wanted to so badly, but I was like,

00:00:51.963 --> 00:00:55.170
the jokester in me, the like Sagittarius,

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.878
just like prankster was
just like, yes I am Mila

00:00:58.878 --> 00:01:02.064
and Natalie and I had
a secret relationship

00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:06.300
when we were filming and
just start a bunch of rumors.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.133
And then I was like, nope,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.993
Sarah, hold your tongue
for one time in your life.

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:13.640
Hold your tongue. And I just,
I just said, no, thanks.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.040
And walked away.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.690
- I'm gonna be real with
you, that's horrible though.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.062
Like, I know y'all do look
a lot alike, but like,

00:01:20.062 --> 00:01:23.140
if you're like interviewing
people on the carpet of the

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.240
Golden Globes, you should
know who you're talking to.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.379
Like, that's horrible.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:29.910
- They were just like screaming at me.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.030
They just thought I was her.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.170
And I was like, oh, these
people want to talk.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.880
Oh, you think I'm Mila? Nevermind.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:35.713
- Oh my God.

00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:38.440
I just know that she's so
much more important than I am

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.120
and always will be and
I admire her so much.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.010
- That is not true.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.410
I love that she was complimented
though she was like,

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.017
you're younger than me. I'll take it.

00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:49.360
So wait, do you have any big
plans for 2021 since 2020

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.751
just really sucked.

00:01:50.751 --> 00:01:53.780
- Well, I would like to say first is,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.140
I don't think that 2021
is a restart button,

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.505
but hopefully some amazing
things project-wise will be

00:02:00.505 --> 00:02:02.223
coming out.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.430
I'm definitely going to get
married this year though.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.520
Like, no matter what,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.814
even if it's signing
paperwork on a kitchen table.

00:02:08.814 --> 00:02:11.510
I'm getting married this year.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.910
- I know you've had to postpone it, right.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.026
Because of COVID obviously.

00:02:15.026 --> 00:02:18.820
- Along with all of the other 2020 brides.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.930
- Yeah. There's been so many.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.050
It was like, I guess somebody
was like it's a lucky year.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.323
And then like, nope.

00:02:25.455 --> 00:02:29.857
- Nope, 2020 is hindsight. I guess.

00:02:29.857 --> 00:02:31.572
- Someone's behind.

00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:35.630
So 2020 was obviously a
dumpster fire for everyone.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:36.980
But how did you handle it?

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.595
Did you, do you get any new,
like hobbies or anything?

00:02:40.595 --> 00:02:43.440
- I told myself I was
going to get to new hobbies

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.260
and then Netflix happened, and food.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.680
No, I, for me, I've been through,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.500
this is not my first
time quarantining before,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.400
when I've had transplants
in the past afterwards,

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.821
you were on such major
immunosuppressants that you had like

00:03:03.821 --> 00:03:07.130
a deficit of an immune system.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.970
So I've had to quarantine
before, definitely not this long,

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.570
only like three months at a time.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:18.110
But so for me I was like chilling
with it. I was like, okay,

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.050
go with the flow. I've done this before.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.860
But like everybody, you know,

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.470
everyone has a limit and there
are times where I feel like

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.870
I'm going absolutely insane.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.520
And I feel like I have zero
purpose for life in the sense of

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.700
like, what am I supposed to be doing?

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.130
I feel like, Nina in
The Seagull, but for me,

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.470
I try to find the silver lining in things.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.440
I think 2020 has been

00:03:42.693 --> 00:03:45.512
an amazing year for people actually

00:03:45.512 --> 00:03:49.230
uniting and standing up for one another,

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.344
especially when it comes
to social injustices.

00:03:52.344 --> 00:03:56.630
I think that has just been
the highlight of my 2020.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.823
It is so beautiful to not only
witness, but be a part of,

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.740
and yeah, I like to
look at silver linings.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:08.640
I'm also a crazy control
freak. So for me --

00:04:10.093 --> 00:04:12.037
- Thar's the Sagittarius by the way.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.830
- Yeah.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:15.833
Monica Geller.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.220
So I like to,

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.439
I like to do things that I at
least have some control over

00:04:25.439 --> 00:04:26.545
and I let,

00:04:26.545 --> 00:04:29.570
I let myself go a little bit
at the beginning of quarantine.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.990
Cause I was like vacation, I
get to eat whatever I want.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.240
I don't ever have to
wash my face ever again.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.480
And then I realized I'm
still engaged and I had to,

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.120
and it was starting to smell.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:45.120
So I ended up finding amazing
skincare routines and just

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.480
something like that really helps me.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.733
I picked up a pen out of nowhere.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.320
- So this is my special
pen. No, but you're right.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.920
Let me, say that because
actually speaking of skincare,

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.660
I will say this a lot of
us have felt like crazy,

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.493
like in this time.

00:05:05.493 --> 00:05:08.330
And I will say like keeping
up some kind of like

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.050
regular routine has it's
helpful for like your

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.510
mental health too, to not
just completely be like,

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.940
so I'm going to stick to just
sweats and never bathing this

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.140
whole time because
what's the point of life.

